  ('d39373e0-60e8-58c0-92c1-d716d141e4db', null, array['42']::text[], '**The correct answer is 42.** Line r has slope $m_{r} = (13 - 12)/(7 - 3) = 1/4$, so any line perpendicular to r has slope $m_{s} = -4$. The line s through $(1,2)$ with slope $-4$ is $y - 2 = -4(x - 1)$, so $y = -4x + 6$. Substitute $y$ into the given form $ax + 7y = c$: $ax + 7(-4x + 6) = c$, which simplifies to $(a - 28)x + 42 = c$. Because $c$ is constant for all $x$, the coefficient of $x$ must be 0, so $a = 28$ and $c = 42$.
