  ('4fdfad5f-c4e3-56a7-abec-0d362bd005e6', null, array['61/65']::text[], '**The correct answer is 61/65.** There are 65 neurons that are not motor neurons (sensory: $12 + 7 + 4 = 23$, interneuron: $10 + 32 + 0 = 42$, so $23 + 42 = 65$). Of those, the ones with diameter ≤ 30 μm are sensory with diameter <20 or 20–30 ($12 + 7 = 19$) and interneurons with diameter <20 or 20–30 ($10 + 32 = 42$), for a total of $19 + 42 = 61$. Thus the conditional probability is $61/65 \approx 0.9385$ (which can be given as $0.94$ or $61/65$).
