  ('9c7c8ed5-8b4b-5f3b-94f8-a59353180d15', 3, null, '**Choice D is correct.** Let the painting’s value at the end of 2017 be $V$. An increase of 179% gives a value $V (1 +$ $1.79) = 2.79V$ at the end of 2018. A subsequent decrease of 27% multiplies that by $0.73$, giving a final value $2.79V \times 0.73 = 2.0367V$, which is $203.67%$ of the original. The net percentage increase is $203.67% -$ $100% = 103.67%$, so choice D is correct.
