  ('20145e8c-b5f5-56e1-bf20-eed6b095559d', 2, null, '**Choice C is correct.** Equation I is $1.5(5x + 3y) = 7.5x + 4.5y = 9$, so it represents the same line as the given equation and therefore the system would have infinitely many solutions (hence at least one). Equation II has a different slope: from $5x + 3y = 6$ we get $y = -\frac{5}{3}x + 2$, and from $7.5x - 4.5y = 4.5$ we get $y = \frac{5}{3}x - 1$. Because the slopes $-\frac{5}{3}$ and $\frac{5}{3}$ are not equal, the lines intersect in exactly one point, so the system also has a solution.
